> Eric Harrison wrote:
>>
>> We were talking about "*Bane" weapons in #nethack and someone brought
>> up the painful nature of insects (specifically soldier ants) and that
>> there should be an "Insectbane".
>>
>> It gave me this silly idea which I thought I'd share with you:
>>
>> The Flyswatter, an artifact hammer that deals double damage against
>> all insects.
>
> One way to nerf the super artifacts is to increase the number of junk
> artifacts.  

Well, this doesn't really "nerf" the good artifacts.  If they're
gamebreakers now, then they're still gamebreakers if you add extra
artifacts -- it's just a tiny bit less likely that they'll be in
one particular game.

Although that does give me a thought -- what if you had to get the
less powerful version of a weapon before getting the high-powered
artifact?  For instance, maybe one outcome of sacrificing (rather
than a new gift) would be to upgrade your wielded weapon; and then
only less-powerful weapons would be available as direct gifts or
through wishing.


